  "notes": "Transcribed 2026-11-11 from the official Southern Utah University 2026-2027 General Catalog (current edition, catoid=28) Aerospace/Aviation Sciences - Fixed-Wing Emphasis (BS) program page and its linked official degree map, 'Aerospace/Aviation Sciences Degree Maps (2026-2027)', Fixed-Wing (Campus) tab, last updated/reviewed August 3, 2026. Semester placement is the university's official sample 4-year campus academic plan (SUU Program Maps, 2026-2027), which the source itself labels a guide only; students confirm specifics in Degree Works with a Student Success Advisor. The catalog prints Total Credits, BS Degree: 120, which the map matches exactly. Every term's courses sum to the map's printed term total (14/15/15/15/15/14/17/15) and the plan to 120. The catalog's Fixed-Wing Curriculum totals 79 credits (Required Core Courses 61, including FIN 2870 Personal Finance and PHYS 1010 Elementary Physics, which also fulfill GE areas as printed; Fixed-Wing Emphasis Courses 18), plus a 28+ credit General Education requirement and a 12-credit BS Degree Requirement in approved mathematics or science (a portion of which may be met by GE Core and Breadth courses, per the catalog); the map's five Free Electives rows total 19 credits. Catalog titles are recorded where the map differs in wording: the map prints AVTN 3440 as 'Human Factors & Aeronautical Decision Making' and PILT 1150 as 'FW Private Certificate ASEL Lab'; the catalog prints 'Human Factors and Aeronautical Decision Making' and 'FW Private Certification ASEL Lab'. Per the catalog, students must complete a minimum of 4 flight labs from SUU, pass an FAA medical exam before beginning flight training, and earn a Student Pilot certificate before beginning a flight lab.",
